{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013xixNB7FJrAPPfvxzDJKJT","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"C03.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Identity-defining artifacts are referenced in deployment config by digest or a version that can't change, not by mutable tags.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open deployment config: Kubernetes manifests, Helm values, Terraform, compose files. 2) Check images use `@sha256:` and prompts, models, and weights use fixed versions. 3) Follow variables and defaults to the final value. 4) Answer no if any reference is a tag like `:latest`, a branch, a model alias, or a default that falls back to one.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"C03.4\",\n  \"check\": \"Self-hosted weights and adapters are checked by digest and signature at load or deploy.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where self-hosted weights and adapters are loaded or deployed (`from_pretrained`, `torch.load`, `safetensors`, download steps). 2) Check a digest compare and a signature check run before use. 3) Answer no if either is missing, wrapped in `try/except` that continues, or a second load path skips it. If only hosted models are used, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"C05.2\",\n  \"check\": \"Model IDs in config are pinned snapshots (plus checkpoint, weights, and adapter versions where supported), not aliases such as 'latest'.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find every model ID in config, env files, and code defaults. 2) Follow env vars to their fallback value. 3) Answer no if any is an alias (`-latest`, undated name), falls back to one when unset, or leaves out the checkpoint, weights, or adapter version where one is used and the provider supports pinning it.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"C05.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Self-hosted weights, adapters, and datasets have their signatures checked against an approved signer before loading, and loading stops if the check fails.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find load paths for self-hosted weights, adapters, and datasets. 2) Check a signature check against an approved signer (for example OpenSSF Model Signing, `cosign verify` with a pinned identity) runs before loading. 3) Answer no if any path skips it, any signer is accepted, or a failure is caught and loading continues. If nothing is self-hosted, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"C05.4\",\n  \"check\": \"Pickle-based model formats are refused at load unless an approved exception and scan are recorded.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Search for pickle-capable loads: `pickle.load`, `torch.load`, `joblib.load`, `.pkl`, `.pt`, `.bin` files. 2) Check the loader refuses these formats unless an approved exception and scan are recorded. 3) Answer no if any pickle-based load runs without that check.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"C05.5\",\n  \"check\": \"The model version the provider or runtime reports serving is recorded separately from the requested model name.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find model call sites and their response handling. 2) Check the served version from the response or runtime (for example the response `model` field) is stored in its own field. 3) Answer no if only the requested name is recorded, or the served field is filled with the requested value.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}] [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER] [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}] [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY] [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS] [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM] [--reas